  "conclusion": "NULL: Weekly returns largely unpredictable OOS. Best OOS R²=0.0097 (RF) but DM t=-1.06 (not significant at Harvey 3.0 threshold). Best model DA=60.9% (RF) barely above base rate 61.9% (market is positive 62% of weeks). No model strategy Sharpe (best=0.99 RF, net of TC) statistically significantly beats BH (0.81). RF's edge comes from being almost always long (97% long) with rare well-timed shorts — not robust predictability. OLS/Ridge/LASSO all have negative OOS R². Consistent with Welch & Goyal (2008): standard predictors fail OOS even at weekly horizon.",
